t $\\left(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1\\right)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in \\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $\\left(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $\\left(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\right).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $\\left(\\frac{4\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3}\\right)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in \\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right),$ and $y=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $\\left(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\right)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d39661f-79dd-50fe-a330-60dbe1bceca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477383} {:answer/id #uuid "8493235e-4c7c-5136-a95e-233e93def0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d39661f-79dd-50fe-a330-60dbe1bceca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477383} :answer-field/id #uuid "158314e9-2e12-5875-addc-2ef5cb84b00e" :answer-field/key "$\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c092fa6-4190-5f6e-96f2-bc83360766b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477385} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ef4cbc-f8fb-5677-bffe-bcc7d3e12bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0ef4cbc-f8fb-5677-bffe-bcc7d3e12bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477386} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f36b3e0-2690-51c8-bea6-a2c585d9ca6f" :answer-field/key "$\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe624146-1ed2-5b35-a3ab-530d859f908b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477387} {:answer/id #uuid "1d3ebb43-05ff-50fc-aa15-d5a2e903731b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d3ebb43-05ff-50fc-aa15-d5a2e903731b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477388} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd01b664-3fa7-5a24-8a4e-c4fe7b0f74ca" :answer-field/key "$(1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477663}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7680c22b-fa61-58ad-8d65-6ff8999855b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-65947" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First, we consider the point $\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(1,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2b8c17c-21b8-507b-8420-d670c4b65f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439459} {:answer/id #uuid "17e98f8a-da18-55f0-8939-1564456b888b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2b8c17c-21b8-507b-8420-d670c4b65f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439459} :answer-field/id #uuid "182f9891-f2da-5a34-881d-2dc0e9bd1216" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,{x}^{2}+x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff01827-2164-503c-885f-729ce07f69b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439461} {:answer/id #uuid "41f3acaf-c391-5b28-bea3-53dc115237b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f3acaf-c391-5b28-bea3-53dc115237b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439462} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6bbea9d-55dc-56d4-af3c-6bb5a3355e6e" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=\\left\\langle -\\frac{y}{4}+x,\\,\\frac{3x}{4}\\right\\rangle $" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35b0a14-7ff3-5770-b606-c1b4ba2b788d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439463} {:answer/id #uuid "c0470289-cbe4-59c9-abaf-f84a85ae4c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0470289-cbe4-59c9-abaf-f84a85ae4c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439464} :answer-field/id #uuid "f690e279-0ebb-573a-bc24-60532b449e8c" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,0⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440089}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0916e138-1ac3-5dc1-b5d3-86d819d37c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-125853" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\left(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\right)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,{x}^{2}+x⟩$ does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x+2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=\\left\\langle -\\frac{y}{4}+x,\\,\\frac{3x}{4}\\right\\rangle $ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{4}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{4},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,0⟩$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F(x,y)=\\left\\langle -\\frac{y}{4}+x,\\,\\frac{3x}{4}\\right\\rangle $; $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,0⟩$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69b927d-fd51-516f-aae0-cf0da09a7720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153881} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ba8dfc-c937-598b-a9a5-dc59f7c01e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153882} {:answer/id #uuid "eb402453-8e9e-5d3c-a06e-96fbfc84d9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153883} {:answer/id #uuid "f418ec1e-ed9d-5bce-a47f-762f1c808098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153884} {:answer/id #uuid "63a0df93-12b0-5a94-8153-cab57c777d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb402453-8e9e-5d3c-a06e-96fbfc84d9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153883} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e9af8f-c53a-563f-b1d5-c1fb676708fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d40b16f4-c022-5679-aaee-aa1be46926d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-149708" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}+4}{5},\\,0<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{20},$ compute $\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1] & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+\\text{E}[1] \\\\  & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3{x}^{2}+4}{5}\\right)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{3}\\right)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{4}\\right)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{20}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]=\\frac{3}{10}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1] & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+1 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{11}{20}-\\frac{3}{10}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0cf51f-5f27-5deb-9c4a-8b592160fb62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448554} {:answer/id #uuid "441b0211-378b-59cc-b36c-e05be34948e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441b0211-378b-59cc-b36c-e05be34948e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448555} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db404e8-6ff4-553a-bd0f-3dc031f6419e" :answer-field/key "$f(x+\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9aa23a-92ec-5956-83f9-5fcc59d04bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448556} {:answer/id #uuid "de73d9ec-e4d9-5bd2-bf7c-8ea7e6908547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de73d9ec-e4d9-5bd2-bf7c-8ea7e6908547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448557} :answer-field/id #uuid "e606f97d-eba3-52ca-87e1-fce3f5ce35ad" :answer-field/key "$f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d98ba68-ec8a-5c5e-ac0f-0008e09c9030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448558} {:answer/id #uuid "273f89b0-161f-5cc9-829e-3d08d1adbdc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d98ba68-ec8a-5c5e-ac0f-0008e09c9030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448558} :answer-field/id #uuid "7635d57d-149c-5b02-be4f-1f0a66eb436b" :answer-field/key "$f\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97cef292-5a85-5947-928d-d07517a20540" :question/math-academy-id "q-338489" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $\\pi $-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $f$ is the $\\pi $-periodic extension of $F,$ we have \n\n- $f(x+\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f(x+\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$” is true. This is exactly the definition of $\\pi $-periodicity: \n\n$$\nf(x+\\pi )=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$” is true. Notice that $F$ itself is $\\pi $-periodic, because for any $x\\in R,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x+\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(x+\\pi ))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+2\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=F(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $F$ already satisfies the periodicity rule, the $\\pi $-periodic extension agrees with $F$ everywhere, so $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement “$f\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$” is false. Since $f$ is $\\pi $-periodic, shifting by $2\\pi $ does not change the value of $f,$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)=f\\left(\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+2\\pi \\right)=f\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBut $f\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)$ does not always equal $f(x).$ For example, take $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=f\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)=F\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)=F\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)\\ne f(x)$ for $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x+\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$”; “$f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e324ed91-4fae-5de5-89d5-cd26e5a4b312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164863} {:answer/id #uuid "740563d1-b2ae-5c42-94a8-321600325c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740563d1-b2ae-5c42-94a8-321600325c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164864} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38d805e-0745-5617-9a20-11b431455d74" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8ddb02b-92cb-56e6-bef2-df860e70ca26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164867} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca0e3e6-336f-55ab-8f04-9f67ade95df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164868} {:answer/id #uuid "2f604df7-206c-51f7-9878-ccf3987ff08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164869} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f44a38-9c4d-555c-8e31-fc73981a0d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ca0e3e6-336f-55ab-8f04-9f67ade95df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164868} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace87305-ddfd-54fb-a584-0e03b68cf02b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164865}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efd96307-00da-56b8-bab1-563e900c1e1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340366" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\left[-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\right]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\pi )-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476227} {:answer/id #uuid "1961d4db-fe56-563a-9283-1c81c4dc846c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476247} {:answer/id #uuid "82eb8742-36e7-5ffd-a6f6-69aaa4ab4057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\,{e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476492} {:answer/id #uuid "9558bd26-9177-5a95-ae61-67abc43f1a3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)={e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476522} {:answer/id #uuid "95a54a82-53ef-52bd-a12a-f81380aaff75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{2}{\\pi (4{y}^{4}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476227} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96ed7e6-c50b-50a2-b3e6-536e5dec7124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19e2e9e5-da57-56e4-b48b-5d2aa326a248" :question/math-academy-id "q-142856" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}},\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x\\}.$\n\n![](images/0a/0a75ec87c30ea5708201cb76816ea3a806648cec197195994cafbe9d9cf588d1.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $-\\infty <y<\\infty $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }{\\left[-\\frac{1}{x}\\right]}_{x={y}^{2}+1}^{x=b} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }\\left[\\frac{1}{b}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\right] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\left[0-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06caa996-019d-55b8-9b18-5c983270de02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439615} {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2f5e64-32f3-5522-8385-0836cdf1b1de" :answer-field/key "The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0e3f19-9827-5a02-9335-759832aa58f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439617} {:answer/id #uuid "25bf5a5c-a822-56a1-a1c2-c6a5ab56d691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c0e3f19-9827-5a02-9335-759832aa58f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439617} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a3ab15-7920-5551-b932-d3776cb36d30" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $y ∈ \\left(-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2}\\right)$." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a5ad809-5893-5399-b9f3-ad07e3a9d1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439619} {:answer/id #uuid "1518fe23-d68e-51c4-ba9d-5901e8279447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a5ad809-5893-5399-b9f3-ad07e3a9d1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439619} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ce653d-94c4-5b5c-8d40-d92ea9bebea4" :answer-field/key "The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440167}] :question/id #uuid "95d49fd8-cd30-53eb-a4a3-b8a8c0494e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-27660" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Tangent has vertical asymptotes at pi/2+n*pi and range all real numbers. Its domain excludes pi/2+n*pi, rather than n*pi. Only “The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e870738-b0c3-5a45-a958-0a8ab816e8ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190325} {:answer/id #uuid "a6105e5f-10e9-560d-b7e2-58cef8643cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190326} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b9be8a-5521-5f98-8ff2-7e30822d0744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190327} {:answer/id #uuid "fa218f47-8a14-524f-b582-ac051f2f4b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190328} {:answer/id #uuid "6095d4ff-1396-56a8-a23b-76ac5552bb6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7b9be8a-5521-5f98-8ff2-7e30822d0744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190327} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb35035-e4ad-5dfe-8305-ac38b8d7b733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190324}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b377af59-2f66-52f6-af8e-4fb410b37e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-149715" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[5X-2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & 1\\le x<3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[5X-2]=5\\text{E}[X]-2\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\right)|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\right)-0+\\left(\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{1}{16}\\right)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-2] & =5\\text{E}[X]-2 \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b631b03-d5e0-5203-8339-312cbadb383b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302730} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2654b9-5d46-5d94-8204-7c8273b7801a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302830} {:answer/id #uuid "457f5420-4987-5c51-86e7-3831b579e36a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302892} {:answer/id #uuid "f5734ddd-5503-537b-832b-324557268167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c2654b9-5d46-5d94-8204-7c8273b7801a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302830} :answer-field/id #uuid "3339b539-b62b-574b-90cb-4fa72c57245d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cd9439f-f8a3-51a2-8290-f9260d300d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303433} {:answer/id #uuid "b00a8eaa-a3df-5ba6-b664-49049f0c4682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303542} {:answer/id #uuid "f13fbead-07a7-5880-9590-62c2f087b15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303966} {:answer/id #uuid "f7145868-034a-55d2-8476-6c5aa282a882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}" :db